  "structure": {
    "block_count": 36,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "How to Handle Toddler Tantrums When Leaving the Playground",
        "text_sha256": "04bf5268c28cc65ea05a2e1c84aa50f09537434a06f0191b2518634b6cd77794",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "by Heidi Murkoff , author of What to Expect When You're Expecting.",
        "text_sha256": "fe0f379871761f84993fc97638e1be60dfaee98ef922ce30fb241d275bfed786",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "tantrums when leaving the playground",
        "text_sha256": "6a417cf4c70caf6751505abe8678e1fa6d5038a75fc9b3b1a930e0855096d360",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just about every parent has at some point endured a temper tantrum when trying to leave the playground. Here are some strategies to avoid meltdowns.",
        "text_sha256": "2ab7178f04e2991d1b5e30fc055047a7f8feceb6113a81863622d7a43b2963b9",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"My daughter has a fit every time we try to leave the playground. She cries, kicks, collapses on the ground, and generally makes a scene. What should I do?\"",
        "text_sha256": "36b2ea8662872f5e90f6ef05b1374cbec4ca43777d985c22679db5c7fe1ad29c",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "First of all, know you're in good company. Just about every parent has at some point endured a playground-parting temper tantrum . Toddlers have trouble making transitions , especially when the transition means saying bye-bye to the slide, sandbox and swings.",
        "text_sha256": "ee68be0c71b2c7c381b077f4992cd8151f1c655e31e032eee9b78db816d3d134",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You'll get through it — or, ideally, avoid it in the first place — by being calm and clever but still the boss.",
        "text_sha256": "3fe8364280b5d0a03c71be66ea4c96bce1db7d6519f90dacafe3a4b11b506643",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here are some tricks to try to prevent toddler meltdowns when leaving the playground:",
        "text_sha256": "e99a09bd581b11155901f6c3ac7da3ddcf3a3ad6a7608510769509c9a1eed807",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Join in the fun. It will be easier to persuade your little one to stop playing if she doesn't have to do it alone. About 10 minutes before you plan to go, join her on the swings, help her put the finishing touches on her sand castle or ask her to show you how well she can climb on the jungle gym. Then, when it's time to go, you can make the transition together, accompanied by heaps of praise over her accomplishments.",
        "text_sha256": "bcf47f6651280af88cc4888522921b44efc8f92f376ecf1b73c8b5cdff44c14a",
        "word_count": 82
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Give notice. You may dread her response to leaving, but she'll handle it better if she has time to get used to the idea. Give her fair notice that you'll be going, starting with a 10-minute warning. At the five-minute mark, offer another reminder, and ask her to finish up what she's doing.",
        "text_sha256": "95474d4de470229740f63dd57326b5613706a2b83d968003b57afe4ea9267db1",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Stick to your word. Be careful not to let her negotiate more time out of you, because once two more turns on the slide morphs into 10, she'll get the idea that \"we have to go now \" can be turned into \"eventually,\" and you'll set yourself up for a lot of future going-home battles.",
        "text_sha256": "1e4cfd5c3523de59f341cbfed182127a0260eecf0e80bc2069b2ca2a4790b54d",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Make the trip home as fun as the playground (or almost, anyway). Come up with a game to play on the way back — see how many dogs you can spot, or look for pretty flowers, or bring along a favorite toy that she can play with.",
        "text_sha256": "6cda20a311a0b527a9bf16357aaf990fc38965f7cd9ba8984cf58ca29204a2e7",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pack snacks. Be prepared to offer snacks on the road since toddlers often realize they're hungry as soon as the fun is done.",
        "text_sha256": "79f167491f5d4d7cb4af6a5e09850bc6dc3c5b46dcb131d7961ee0ab7c265fad",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Finally, on the way home, let her know what she'll be doing when she gets home — having dinner, making cookies, going to visit Grandma — so she'll know what to expect and will have something else to look forward to.",
        "text_sha256": "b25e644d4ae8de7c7b112bd7d31c563b5148d74f7d381299fae1a30f4e1ed7ed",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Good luck,",
        "text_sha256": "025f1bc4e552180371e36b8972e979b175a33ae7a72003900fd0ce28611e29d9",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Heidi Murkoff",
        "text_sha256": "6f05d1b1394d028842497499fff96bffb14810fb4a10d1a23a1ef1b82a72292e",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
